This is a hex edit by Dominic Alston.I made a few small changes to port it to OSK.  In addition, I added an option to open a directory for editing.  Hex is a wonderful tool.  It lets you view and edit files as a hex dump.  The data may be edited in either the hex or ascii representations.  I found hex to be invaluable in repairing some damage to my file system which had corrupted some filesinto "directories" which could not be deleted by normal methods.In this archive you will find an OSK executable that I made on my 68070 MM/1 for OSK 2.4 using gcc 1.4.2.  The source is, of course, also included.  To build it you will need a UNIX compatability library ( I used the TOP os9.l ) and a curses library ( I used TOP ncurses ). I recommend gmake and gcc although it may work with Microware's non-ANSI C and shittymake - I haven't tried. 	Ed Gow